  "body": "This attribute controls whether various parts of rendering (under a broad definition, which includes referenced-resource loading, custom element upgrades, IntersectionObserver, painting and animations) are run. It is intended as a performance primitive that allows the browser to skip expensive rendering work for offscreen or otherwise not visible content.\r\n\r\nIn addition, a new activation concept is introduced which allows the browser to perform all rendering tasks for content controlled by the `rendersubtree` attribute on which a user-agent feature (such as find-in-page, accessibility or scroll-into-view).\r\n\r\nSee https://github.com/WICG/display-locking/blob/master/explainer-new.md for more details, context and examples.\r\n\r\nAn HTML spec PR will come shortly.\r\n\r\n@vmpstr @domenic @tabatkins @rakina ",
